From b7e8fc646f6b4491237a807998df857dec07d7a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 11:57:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 138/145] media: meson: vdec: hevc: return the input credit for
 a discarded picture

A transport stream joined mid-GOP reaches its first IRAP and then
starves in the middle of the picture after it.  Sampled with the
watchdog off: the IDR arrives 79 slices in, and the firmware then sits
at HEVC_CODED_SLICE_SEGMENT_DAT with the LCU counter frozen at 2021 of
2040, the shifter byte count frozen, and 378 bytes left in the stream
FIFO.  It is not wedged - it is waiting for bitstream, and the same
leftover data every time is why it always stops at the same LCU.

The reason none arrives is in the same sample: esparser_queued_bufs is
80 while the CAPTURE queue allows 17 (a DPB of 1 plus 19 ready, less
the 3 the gate holds back).  Every one of those 79 discarded pictures
took a credit that only amvdec_dst_buf_done() returns, and a discarded
picture produces no frame to return it with, so the counter ends the
skip phase far above the limit and the ESPARSER never feeds again.

Return the credit where the picture is dropped, once per picture -
dependent and continuation slice segments share the credit of the
picture they belong to, so only a first slice segment repays.

Fixes: c493d1097b16 ("media: meson: vdec: hevc: keep a resynchronising decoder alive")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
index 85ca428bbd2d..e05aa878ea06 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -1737,6 +1737,17 @@ static void codec_hevc_process_segment_header(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 static int codec_hevc_skip_slice(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 {
 	struct amvdec_core *core = sess->core;
+	struct codec_hevc *hevc = sess->priv;
+
+	/*
+	 * A discarded picture produces no frame, and a frame is the only
+	 * thing that ever returns the input credit the ESPARSER spent on
+	 * it.  Return it here, once per picture, or a session that
+	 * discards for any length of time leaves the counter above what
+	 * the CAPTURE queue allows and never gets fed again.
+	 */
+	if (hevc->rpm_param.p.first_slice_segment_in_pic_flag)
+		atomic_dec_if_positive(&sess->esparser_queued_bufs);
 
 	amvdec_clear_dos_bits(core, HEVC_WAIT_FLAG, BIT(1));
 	amvdec_write_dos(core, HEVC_DEC_STATUS_REG, HEVC_ACTION_DONE);
-- 
